de1 (primary), node2 and node3 (standbys) on CentOS Stream 10, exercised a full failover (node1 lost -> node2 promoted -> node3 repointed -> node1 rejoined as standby of node2) with zero data loss, and completed the mandatory one-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes with proof of changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed postgresql-server/contrib 16.14 on node1, node2, node3 via dnf\",\"Initialized DB on node1; configured wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders, hot_standby, and pg_hba.conf for replication and client access\",\"Generated the replicator role's password on node1 with openssl and passed it to other nodes only via secret_env, never in literal command text\",\"Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes\",\"Built node2 and node3 as standbys via pg_basebackup -R from node1; verified standby.signal/primary_conninfo and confirmed streaming state with ~0 replication lag\",\"Created a test table and inserted baseline rows; confirmed replication to both standbys\",\"Simulated primary loss: confirmed node2 fully caught up to node1's WAL LSN, then stopped postgresql on node1\",\"Promoted node2 to writable primary via pg_ctl promote; verified zero data loss (all pre-failover rows present) and that new writes succeed on node2\",\"Repointed node3's primary_conninfo to node2 and restarted it as a standby of the new primary; verified streaming and full data consistency\",\"Rebuilt node1 via pg_basebackup -R from node2 and started it as a standby of node2; verified recovery mode and intact data\",\"Captured boot_id and health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Rebooted node1, then node3, then node2 (the primary) one at a time via systemctl reboot, polling each node until exec access returned\",\"Proved each restart via changed /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id (not just elapsed time or service state)\",\"Verified post-restart recovery for each node: node1 and node3 resumed streaming as standbys with full data; node2 resumed as writable primary, accepted a new write, and both standbys replicated it\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Primary/standby streaming replication configured node1->node2/node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a60f35fbaa14ed1\",\"cmd-1e2e88ea47f640d3\",\"cmd-4b22733dac644af4\",\"cmd-533a378acba54ca0\",\"cmd-6915c653dee14bac\",\"cmd-9c02a2231e284985\",\"cmd-1fa2429557ec49dc\",\"cmd-eb2845971c7f4fcf\"],\"summary\":\"postgresql installed and initialized on node1; replication settings and replicator role created; node2/node3 built via pg_basebackup -R with standby.signal and primary_conninfo pointing at node1; pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys streaming\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replicated data verified consistent before disruption\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-06ab1365076547bb\",\"cmd-4bc7750b9f984464\",\"cmd-b6e0fe2289e14eff\"],\"summary\":\"Rows inserted on node1 primary appear identically on node2 and node3 standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"Primary loss simulated and standby promoted without data loss\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a1add77623d6451c\",\"cmd-8869a82d6b794a4d\",\"cmd-3d2f5e87467b4bba\",\"cmd-82a59774613b4322\",\"cmd-b1bad789c8254e89\"],\"summary\":\"node2 confirmed at matching WAL LSN before node1 was stopped; node2 promoted to primary (pg_is_in_recovery=f) and accepted a new write while retaining all prior rows including the last one written on node1 pre-failover\"},{\"requirement\":\"Remaining standby (node3) repointed to new primary\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-796fbd1ed6234131\",\"cmd-082804476bd04315\",\"cmd-c364a508c33b40f3\"],\"summary\":\"node3 primary_conninfo updated to node2, restarted, confirmed streaming from node2 in pg_stat_replication and holding the post-failover row\"},{\"requirement\":\"Recovered former primary (node1) rejoins as standby of current primary (node2)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-070c650445e843ff\",\"cmd-254a3259c2ff42ec\",\"cmd-14a490843ec6409d\",\"cmd-eafe822fa01a479d\"],\"summary\":\"node1 rebuilt via pg_basebackup -R from node2, started as standby (pg_is_in_recovery=t) with full data, and node2's pg_stat_replication shows both node1 and node3 streaming\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3819516629aa431c\",\"cmd-0353bb34eaaa4d07\",\"cmd-16b554886f7f4380\",\"cmd-d6d8cf175a694ba7\",\"cmd-8dd1450f91654130\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4d340bf4...; systemctl reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id 9c54dcf4... (changed); postgresql active, standby recovery mode confirmed, all rows present, node2 shows node1 streaming again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8fd7a9c7b3934ed5\",\"cmd-58c311fab14a433e\",\"cmd-b113a37dc82f4233\",\"cmd-88f75b7dce1c4e7d\",\"cmd-8148d71c0e484fba\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4d842549...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id 26c0dbdc... (changed); postgresql active, standby recovery mode confirmed, all rows present, node2 shows node3 streaming again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (primary) restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state as primary\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6eae4d49d19d4586\",\"cmd-4ff5db7464674024\",\"cmd-5e86233cedb84425\",\"cmd-eb78169cfb694bfd\",\"cmd-f34a20749a784646\",\"cmd-a103fffe443c47ef\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id cce73776...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id abf60f22... (changed); postgresql resumed active as writable primary (pg_is_in_recovery=f), accepted a new write, and both node1 and node3 replicated the new row, proving full cluster recovery\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2 and node3 (standbys) on CentOS Stream 10, exercised a full failover (node1 lost -> node2 promoted -> node3 repointed -> node1 rejoined as standby of node2) with zero data loss, and completed the mandatory one-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes with proof of changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery.","actions_performed":["Installed postgresql-server/contrib 16.14 on node1, node2, node3 via dnf","Initialized DB on node1; configured wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders, hot_standby, and pg_hba.conf for replication and client access","Generated the replicator role's password on node1 with openssl and passed it to other nodes only via secret_env, never in literal command text","Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes","Built node2 and node3 as standbys via pg_basebackup -R from node1; verified standby.signal/primary_conninfo and confirmed streaming state with ~0 replication lag","Created a test table and inserted baseline rows; confirmed replication to both standbys","Simulated primary loss: confirmed node2 fully caught up to node1's WAL LSN, then stopped postgresql on node1","Promoted node2 to writable primary via pg_ctl promote; verified zero data loss (all pre-failover rows present) and that new writes succeed on node2","Repointed node3's primary_conninfo to node2 and restarted it as a standby of the new primary; verified streaming and full data consistency","Rebuilt node1 via pg_basebackup -R from node2 and started it as a standby of node2; verified recovery mode and intact data","Captured boot_id and health baseline on all three nodes","Rebooted node1, then node3, then node2 (the primary) one at a time via systemctl reboot, polling each node until exec access returned","Proved each restart via changed /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id (not just elapsed time or service state)","Verified post-restart recovery for each node: node1 and node3 resumed streaming as standbys with full data; node2 resumed as writable primary, accepted a new write, and both standbys replicated it"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Primary/standby streaming replication configured node1->node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-2a60f35fbaa14ed1","cmd-1e2e88ea47f640d3","cmd-